## CHORUS BROTHERS — the moneylender's (`story.ni:5425-5450`) — the room.
## ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

create the Chorus Brothers
  a room
  aka moneylenders shop, moneylender's shop, moneylenders, moneylender's, chorus brothers shop
  west to the Lord's Market, one-way

  The inside of this shop is dark — dark wood paneling on the walls; deep,
  wine-dark carpeting on the floor; even a pair of huge, leather armchairs
  over in one corner. The back half of the room is hidden behind a wall of
  reinforced wood, with a wide window cut through the center.

create the armchairs
  aka armchair, chair, chairs, leather armchairs, leather chairs
  scenery, plural
  in the Chorus Brothers

  The armchairs are overstuffed, upholstered in rich, dark leather.

  on the player entering
    refuse armchairs-awkward
  end on

create the moneylender's carpet
  aka carpet, carpeting, wine-dark carpet
  scenery
  in the Chorus Brothers

  (TODO during play-testing — the carpet has no description in the source; a
  line or none, David's call.)

create the teller's window
  aka window, tellers window, counter, grating, brass grating, grate, reinforced wall, wall
  scenery
  in the Chorus Brothers

  The window forms a sort of counter, with an ornately scrolled, brass grating
  that opens to the inside, allowing customers to speak with the proprietors
  on the other side. In fact, it appears that the only way to get service here
  is by standing up at the counter, so it's not exactly clear what the fancy
  chairs are for.

define phrase armchairs-awkward
  They look very comfortable, but it would feel awkward sitting in the chair
  and yelling across the room at the counter.
end phrase

## ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
## THE BACK ALLEY (`story.ni:5607`) — where the chapter ends. Entering it for
## the first time is Chapter 3's opening beat; Bobby, the coin trick and the
## Maiden House street are Chapter 3's. The room stands so the square's
## south exit is real.
## ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

create the Back Alley
  a room
  aka alley, back alley, shortcut, short cut

  A little-known shortcut between Lord's Market and the less affluent
  neighborhoods of the city's south end. A narrow street to the southwest
  leads to Maiden House, or you can return to the market square to the north.
